Fix kmalloc-64 slab leak: free the semaphore-surface callback on the
NVOS_STATUS_ERROR_ALREADY_SIGNALLED path of
nvKmsKapiRegisterSemaphoreSurfaceCallback().

When RM's _semsurfAddWaiter() finds the semaphore already past wait_value
it returns NV_ERR_ALREADY_SIGNALLED before registerEventNotification(),
so the freshly allocated NvKmsKapiSemaphoreSurfaceCallback (40 bytes ->
kmalloc-64) is never stored in any RM list and never handed back to the
caller (*pCallbackHandle unwritten). nvidia-drm's reg_callbacks retry
loop (do/while on NVKMS_KAPI_REG_WAITER_ALREADY_SIGNALLED in
nvidia-drm-fence.c) then allocates a fresh one per iteration; under
Wayland explicit-sync compositing this races constantly (~50/s observed)
and grows unreclaimable slab by hundreds of MiB/day until the host
livelocks. The orphaned objects are unreachable from every teardown path
(fence signal, DRM fd close, module unload) so only a reboot recovers
the memory.

Freeing cb here is safe by construction: on this status RM provably
never retained the notification handle and the caller never receives the
pointer, so no double-free or dangling reference is possible. This
mirrors the existing unconditional nvKmsKapiFree(cb) at the fail: label.

Verified byte-identical buggy code at tags 595.80, 595.84, 610.43.03.

--- a/src/nvidia-modeset/kapi/src/nvkms-kapi-sync.c
+++ b/src/nvidia-modeset/kapi/src/nvkms-kapi-sync.c
@@ -445,6 +445,18 @@
         }
         return NVKMS_KAPI_REG_WAITER_SUCCESS;
     case NVOS_STATUS_ERROR_ALREADY_SIGNALLED:
+        /*
+         * RM detected the semaphore already passed wait_value and bailed out
+         * of _semsurfAddWaiter() before registerEventNotification(), so the
+         * notification handle in cb->rmCallback was never stored anywhere and
+         * *pCallbackHandle is never written on this path: cb is unreachable
+         * by both RM and the caller. Free it here, exactly as the fail: path
+         * does, or every ALREADY_SIGNALLED race (one per iteration of
+         * nvidia-drm's reg_callbacks retry loop) leaks one kmalloc-64 object
+         * into unreclaimable slab. nvKmsKapiFree(NULL) is a no-op for the
+         * pCallback == NULL case.
+         */
+        nvKmsKapiFree(cb);
         return NVKMS_KAPI_REG_WAITER_ALREADY_SIGNALLED;
     default:
         break;
